fix: review round 7 -- shared-VM-disk model, filesystem hard-stop, physical-free-space emergency eviction, docker launch mode, cache-miss matrix, locale-drift CI guard

Context (operator correction): the 1.5 TB budget is NOT a dedicated NVMe; it is
a slice of the SHARED VM disk that also carries Docker images, model weights and
the OS. All "pinned NVMe" wording across repo + wiki (EN/RU/ZH) now says
"shared VM disk", with a >=50 GB free-space headroom rule for non-cache writers.

Review items:
1. Docs/test-count drift: 29/49 mentions all synced to the real count (52
   pytest-collected unit tests) in README x3, wiki Home/FAQ x2, final-report.
   LICENSE wording ("Anyone using...") corrected: Apache-2.0 s.4(d) binds
   DISTRIBUTORS (forks/mirrors/bundles/services), not internal end users -- now
   stated in README x3 and NOTICE.
2A. Security hardening: docs/security x3 + README -- loopback is NOT auth; UDS
   (0600) or local Bearer token for multi-tenant/Kubernetes contexts.
2B. Logical budget vs physical disk: kvpersist.cli gains `free` (physical
   free-space report) and `emergency-evict` (forced LRU-style namespace eviction
   when physical free space < 5 GB, regardless of logical budget);
   budget-report.sh prints physical_free_gb + warning; storage-management.md
   documents the emergency-eviction mechanism + required hardware test.
2C. Network FS = HARD STOP in preflight (die, not warn) on nfs/cifs/smb/fuse:
   atomic-rename semantics and small-file performance require a local POSIX FS.
3A. Docker launch mode: scripts/start-cache.sh accepts KVP_LAUNCH_MODE=docker
   to run `lmcache server` inside the same pinned vLLM image (same Python/
   PyTorch -> no host ABI/version friction at all); host-venv mode unchanged.
3B. Cache Miss Matrix: wiki Troubleshooting x3 -- table of every identity field
   whose change rotates the namespace (weights content, revision, tokenizer,
   template, dtype, max-model-len, TP, KV geometry, connector version, image
   digest, engine flags) so "cache went cold after my tweak" is expected, not a
   bug.
3C. tests/test_docs_sync.py (CI guard): every EN config knob must be documented
   in RU/ZH siblings, localized files must not invent knobs, docs must not
   reference knobs the configs do not define.

Also: verify-engine-identity pre-flight step added to wiki Recipes-Integration
(prod KV_PERSIST=1 path), consistent with the rest of the docs.